{"title":"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:25)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:25)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A fair coin is tossed 3 times. What is the probability of at least two consecutive heads?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/2/a82f8ba3c6d1d786b69b68dda01be5471d832bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\frac{1}{8} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\frac{3}{8} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"343\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591d9b115cf384bfadec71afd7ffa4397726d79a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 = 8$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> ways to flip the coins, in order.\nThere are two ways to get exactly two consecutive heads: HHT and THH.\nThere is only one way to get three consecutive heads: HHH.\nTherefore, the probability of flipping at least two consecutive heads is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27cdde6a9de68c5239914a9514688224c3da5fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\frac{3}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"55\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complementary_counting\" title=\"Complementary counting\">complementary counting</a>. To start with, the unfavorable outcomes (in this case, not getting 2 consecutive heads) are: TTT, HTH, and THT. The probability of these three outcomes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, respectively. So the rest is exactly the probability of flipping at least two consecutive heads: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60cab2203737b2809998d2e002d2580794e3d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{3}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" />. It is the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27cdde6a9de68c5239914a9514688224c3da5fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\frac{3}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"55\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~LarryFlora\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can list out all the ways to flip a coin three times: HHH,HHT,HTH,THH,HTT,THT,TTH,TTT. Out of them, only HHH,HHT,THH, have at least two consecutive heads. Since there are three ways to flip at least two consecutive heads, and eight total choices, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27cdde6a9de68c5239914a9514688224c3da5fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\frac{3}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"55\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~andliu766\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:25.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:25)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:25)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:25)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/3cnFBKJUBG0\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/3cnFBKJUBG0</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p><p>Note: the problem where this is linked is covered 1:50-2:15\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2lynqd2bRZY\">https://youtu.be/2lynqd2bRZY</a> ~savannahsolver\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6xNkyDgIhEE?t=44\">https://youtu.be/6xNkyDgIhEE?t=44</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 8\">2013 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8